{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/tmygso","slideIndex":4,"text":"Three further directions extend this workflow. **Practice:** lock the selection, pick up the instrument, hear a model, wait a user-set interval and repeat, with count-in and immediate Stop. The selection stays available when hands leave the page. Amber Sound Touch describes teaching through short demonstrations and repeated playing. **Annotations:** bind the original voice recording to the piece, part and measure, including teacher or conductor advice. Readers choose query, arrival or pre-practice review. **Independent setup:** announce page and tracking status, give an actionable recovery cue, and allow a spoken measure number. Clearly distinguish the current location from the last valid location. Voice, earcons and optional haptics can be compared."}